{"title": "Sectional Mock #122 (Mixed)", "duration_min": 30.0, "questions": [{"q_en": "<p>In a 1500 m race, bike A beats bike B by 300 m. bike B beats bike C by 200 m in a 900 m race. If bike A beats bike C by 30 seconds in a 1350 m race, then what is the speed of bike C?</p>", "q_hi": "<p>1500 &#2350;&#2368;&#2335;&#2352; &#2325;&#2368; &#2342;&#2380;&#2337;&#2364; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306;, &#2348;&#2366;&#2311;&#2325; A, &#2348;&#2366;&#2311;&#2325; B &#2360;&#2375; 300 &#2350;&#2368;&#2335;&#2352; &#2310;&#2327;&#2375; &#2344;&#2367;&#2325;&#2354; &#2332;&#2366;&#2340;&#2368; &#2361;&#2376;&#2404; 900 &#2350;&#2368;&#2335;&#2352; &#2325;&#2368; &#2342;&#2380;&#2337;&#2364; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2348;&#2366;&#2311;&#2325; B, &#2348;&#2366;&#2311;&#2325; C &#2360;&#2375; 200 &#2350;&#2368;&#2335;&#2352; &#2310;&#2327;&#2375; &#2344;&#2367;&#2325;&#2354; &#2332;&#2366;&#2340;&#2368; &#2361;&#2376;&#2404; &#2351;&#2342;&#2367; 1350 &#2350;&#2368;&#2335;&#2352; &#2325;&#2368; &#2342;&#2380;&#2337;&#2364; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2348;&#2366;&#2311;&#2325; A, &#2348;&#2366;&#2311;&#2325; C &#2360;&#2375; 30 &#2360;&#2375;&#2325;&#2306;&#2337; &#2310;&#2327;&#2375; &#2344;&#2367;&#2325;&#2354; &#2332;&#2366;&#2340;&#2368; &#2361;&#2376;, &#2340;&#2379; &#2348;&#2366;&#2311;&#2325; C &#2325;&#2368; &#2327;&#2340;&#2367; &#2325;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366; &#2361;&#2376;?</p>", "options_en": ["17 m/sec", "19 m/sec", "15 m/sec", "13 m/sec"], "options_hi": ["17 &#2350;&#2368;&#2335;&#2352;/&#2360;&#2375;&#2325;&#2306;&#2337;", "19 &#2350;&#2368;&#2335;&#2352;/&#2360;&#2375;&#2325;&#2306;&#2337;", "15 &#2350;&#2368;&#2335;&#2352;/&#2360;&#2375;&#2325;&#2306;&#2337;", "13 &#2350;&#2368;&#2335;&#2352;/&#2360;&#2375;&#2325;&#2306;&#2337;"], "answer": 0, "solution_en": "<p>When bike A covers 1500 m bike B covers 1200 m</p><p>The ratio of speed = 5: 4</p><p>When bike B covers 900 m bike C covers 700 m</p><p>The ratio of speed = 9: 7</p><p>The ratio of A, B, and C = 45 : 36: 28</p><p>When bike A covers 1350 m, C covers = 1350 * 28/45 = 840 m</p><p>So, difference = 1350  -  840 = 510</p><p>Bike C will cover the remaining 510 m in 30 seconds</p><p>Hence, the speed of bike C = 510/30 = 17 m/sec</p>", "solution_hi": "<p>When bike A covers 1500 m bike B covers 1200 m</p><p>The ratio of speed = 5: 4</p><p>When bike B covers 900 m bike C covers 700 m</p><p>The ratio of speed = 9: 7</p><p>The ratio of A, B, and C = 45 : 36: 28</p><p>When bike A covers 1350 m, C covers = 1350 * 28/45 = 840 m</p><p>So, difference = 1350  -  840 = 510</p><p>Bike C will cover the remaining 510 m in 30 seconds</p><p>Hence, the speed of bike C = 510/30 = 17 m/sec</p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25, "chap": "Time, Speed & Distance"}, {"q_en": "<p>If n is an even prime number, then which of the following is a perfect square? </p>", "q_hi": "<p>&#2360;&#2348;&#2360;&#2375; &#2348;&#2337;&#2364;&#2368; &#2324;&#2352; &#2360;&#2348;&#2360;&#2375; &#2331;&#2379;&#2335;&#2368; &#2330;&#2366;&#2352; &#2309;&#2306;&#2325;&#2379;&#2306; &#2325;&#2368; &#2360;&#2306;&#2326;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366;&#2323;&#2306; &#2325;&#2366; &#2351;&#2379;&#2327; &#2332;&#2381;&#2334;&#2366;&#2340; &#2325;&#2352;&#2375;&#2306; &#2332;&#2379; 4 &#2360;&#2375; &#2358;&#2369;&#2352;&#2370; &#2361;&#2379;&#2340;&#2368; &#2361;&#2376;&#2306; &#2324;&#2352; 2 &#2346;&#2352; &#2360;&#2350;&#2366;&#2346;&#2381;&#2340; &#2361;&#2379;&#2340;&#2368; &#2361;&#2376;&#2306;&#2404;</p>", "options_en": ["n(2n  -  1)", "n(n + 1)(n + 2)", "(n + 1)(2n  -  1)", "n<sup>3</sup>(n  -  1)"], "options_hi": ["8844", "9044", "9124", "8994"], "answer": 3, "solution_en": "<p>For odd value of (a + b)(c + d) =&gt; (a + b) and (c + d) must be odd.</p><p>Since, a and c are even, then b and d must be odd integers.</p>", "solution_hi": "<p>For odd value of (a + b)(c + d) =&gt; (a + b) and (c + d) must be odd.</p><p>Since, a and c are even, then b and d must be odd integers.</p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25, "chap": "Number System"}, {"q_en": "<p>Find the equation of the sphere having centre (2, -1, 4) and the radius of 5 units.</p>", "q_hi": "<p>&#2325;&#2375;&#2306;&#2342;&#2381;&#2352; (2, -1, 4) &#2324;&#2352; 5 &#2311;&#2325;&#2366;&#2312; &#2340;&#2381;&#2352;&#2367;&#2332;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366; &#2357;&#2366;&#2354;&#2375; &#2327;&#2379;&#2354;&#2375; &#2325;&#2366; &#2360;&#2350;&#2368;&#2325;&#2352;&#2339; &#2332;&#2381;&#2334;&#2366;&#2340; &#2325;&#2368;&#2332;&#2367;&#2319;&#2404;</p>", "options_en": ["x<sup>2</sup> + y<sup>2</sup> + z<sup>2</sup> + 4x + 2y  -  8z  -  6 = 0", "x<sup>2</sup> + y<sup>2</sup> + z<sup>2</sup>  -  6x + 2y  -  9z  -  4 = 0", "x<sup>2</sup> + y<sup>2</sup> + z<sup>2</sup> + 5x + 2y  -  6z  -  8 = 0", "x<sup>2</sup> + y<sup>2</sup> + z<sup>2</sup>  -  4x + 2y  -  8z  -  4 = 0"], "options_hi": ["x<sup>2</sup> + y<sup>2</sup> + z<sup>2</sup> + 4x + 2y - 8z - 6 = 0", "x<sup>2</sup> + y<sup>2</sup> + z<sup>2</sup> - 6x + 2y - 9z - 4 = 0", "x<sup>2</sup> + y<sup>2</sup> + z<sup>2</sup> + 5x + 2y - 6z - 8 = 0", "x<sup>2</sup> + y<sup>2</sup> + z<sup>2</sup> - 4x + 2y - 8z - 4 = 0"], "answer": 3, "solution_en": "<p>Points of centre = (x<sub>0</sub>, y<sub>0</sub>, z<sub>0</sub>) = (2, -1, 4)</p><p>Radius = R = 5 units</p><p>General equation of sphere =&gt;</p><p>(x  -  x<sub>0</sub>)<sup>2</sup> + (y  -  y<sub>0</sub>)<sup>2</sup> +(z  -  z<sub>0</sub>)<sup>2</sup> = R<sup>2</sup></p><p>(x  -  2)<sup>2</sup> + [y  -  (-1)]<sup>2</sup> +(z  -  4)<sup>2</sup> = 5<sup>2</sup></p><p>x<sup>2</sup> + 4  -  4x + y<sup>2</sup> + 1 + 2y + z<sup>2</sup> + 16  -  8z = 25</p><p>x<sup>2</sup> + y<sup>2</sup> + z<sup>2</sup>  -  4x + 2y  -  8z  -  4 = 0</p>", "solution_hi": "<p>Points of centre = (x<sub>0</sub>, y<sub>0</sub>, z<sub>0</sub>) = (2, -1, 4)</p><p>Radius = R = 5 units</p><p>General equation of sphere =&gt;</p><p>(x  -  x<sub>0</sub>)<sup>2</sup> + (y  -  y<sub>0</sub>)<sup>2</sup> +(z  -  z<sub>0</sub>)<sup>2</sup> = R<sup>2</sup></p><p>(x  -  2)<sup>2</sup> + [y  -  (-1)]<sup>2</sup> +(z  -  4)<sup>2</sup> = 5<sup>2</sup></p><p>x<sup>2</sup> + 4  -  4x + y<sup>2</sup> + 1 + 2y + z<sup>2</sup> + 16  -  8z = 25</p><p>x<sup>2</sup> + y<sup>2</sup> + z<sup>2</sup>  -  4x + 2y  -  8z  -  4 = 0</p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25, "chap": "Mensuration (2D)"}, {"q_en": "<p>In a circle two chords AB and CD intersect at point O. If AO = 14 cm, BO = 21 cm and CO = 15 cm. what is the length of CD?</p>", "q_hi": "<p>&#2319;&#2325; &#2357;&#2371;&#2340;&#2381;&#2340; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2342;&#2379; &#2332;&#2368;&#2357;&#2366;&#2319;&#2305; AB &#2324;&#2352; CD &#2348;&#2367;&#2306;&#2342;&#2369; O &#2346;&#2352; &#2346;&#2381;&#2352;&#2340;&#2367;&#2330;&#2381;&#2331;&#2375;&#2342; &#2325;&#2352;&#2340;&#2368; &#2361;&#2376;&#2306;&#2404; &#2351;&#2342;&#2367; AO = 14 &#2360;&#2375;&#2350;&#2368;, BO = 21 &#2360;&#2375;&#2350;&#2368; &#2324;&#2352; CO = 15 &#2360;&#2375;&#2350;&#2368; &#2361;&#2376;&#2404; CD &#2325;&#2368; &#2354;&#2306;&#2348;&#2366;&#2312; &#2325;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366; &#2361;&#2376;?</p>", "options_en": ["38.6 cm", "35.6 cm", "40.6 cm", "34.6 cm"], "options_hi": ["38.6 &#2360;&#2375;&#2350;&#2368;", "35.6 &#2360;&#2375;&#2350;&#2368;", "40.6 &#2360;&#2375;&#2350;&#2368;", "34.6 &#2360;&#2375;&#2350;&#2368;"], "answer": 3, "solution_en": "<p><img width=190 height=172 id=\"Picture 17\" src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p24543/image005.png\"></p><p>AO * BO = CO * DO</p><p>14 * 21 = 15 * DO</p><p>DO = 19.6 cm</p><p>CD = 15 + 19.6 = 34.6 cm</p>", "solution_hi": "<p><img width=190 height=172 id=\"Picture 17\" src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p24543/image005.png\"></p><p>AO * BO = CO * DO</p><p>14 * 21 = 15 * DO</p><p>DO = 19.6 cm</p><p>CD = 15 + 19.6 = 34.6 cm</p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25, "chap": "Mensuration (2D)"}, {"q_en": "<p>In a 750 m race, X runs at 15 km/h. X gives Y a head start of 30 m and still beats him by 60 seconds. Find the speed of X.</p>", "q_hi": "<p>750 &#2350;&#2368;&#2335;&#2352; &#2325;&#2368; &#2342;&#2380;&#2337;&#2364; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306;, X 15 &#2325;&#2367;&#2350;&#2368;/&#2328;&#2306;&#2335;&#2366; &#2325;&#2368; &#2327;&#2340;&#2367; &#2360;&#2375; &#2342;&#2380;&#2337;&#2364;&#2340;&#2366; &#2361;&#2376;&#2404; X, Y &#2360;&#2375; 30 &#2350;&#2368;&#2335;&#2352; &#2310;&#2327;&#2375; &#2352;&#2361;&#2340;&#2366; &#2361;&#2376; &#2324;&#2352; &#2347;&#2367;&#2352; &#2349;&#2368; &#2313;&#2360;&#2375; 60 &#2360;&#2375;&#2325;&#2306;&#2337; &#2360;&#2375; &#2361;&#2352;&#2366; &#2342;&#2375;&#2340;&#2366; &#2361;&#2376;&#2404; X &#2325;&#2368; &#2327;&#2340;&#2367; &#2332;&#2381;&#2334;&#2366;&#2340; &#2325;&#2368;&#2332;&#2367;&#2319;&#2404;</p>", "options_en": ["9.6 km/h", "12.4 km/h", "10.8 km/h", "8.4 km/h"], "options_hi": ["9.6 &#2325;&#2367;&#2350;&#2368;/&#2328;&#2306;&#2335;&#2366;", "12.4 &#2325;&#2367;&#2350;&#2368;/&#2328;&#2306;&#2335;&#2366;", "10.8 &#2325;&#2367;&#2350;&#2368;/&#2328;&#2306;&#2335;&#2366;", "8.4 &#2325;&#2367;&#2350;&#2368;/&#2328;&#2306;&#2335;&#2366;"], "answer": 2, "solution_en": "<p><b>[To convert km/h in m/s, multiply with 5/18]</b></p><p>15 km/h = 75/18 m/s</p><p>Time taken by X to cover 750 m = 750/(75/18) = 180 seconds</p><p>Distance covered by Y = 750  -  30 = 720 m</p><p>Time taken by Y to cover 720 m = 180 + 60 = 240 seconds</p><p>Hence, the speed of Y = 720/ 240 = 3 m/s = 3 * 18/5 = 10.8 km/h</p>", "solution_hi": "<p><b>[To convert km/h in m/s, multiply with 5/18]</b></p><p>15 km/h = 75/18 m/s</p><p>Time taken by X to cover 750 m = 750/(75/18) = 180 seconds</p><p>Distance covered by Y = 750  -  30 = 720 m</p><p>Time taken by Y to cover 720 m = 180 + 60 = 240 seconds</p><p>Hence, the speed of Y = 720/ 240 = 3 m/s = 3 * 18/5 = 10.8 km/h</p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25, "chap": "Time, Speed & Distance"}, {"q_en": "<p>When a number is divided by a certain divisor, the remainder is 48, and another no. is divided by the same divisor, the remainder is 33. If the sum of both numbers is divided by the same certain divisor, the remainder is 29. Find the certain divisor.</p>", "q_hi": "<p>&#2332;&#2348; &#2319;&#2325; &#2360;&#2306;&#2326;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366; &#2325;&#2379; &#2319;&#2325; &#2344;&#2367;&#2358;&#2381;&#2330;&#2367;&#2340; &#2349;&#2366;&#2332;&#2325; &#2360;&#2375; &#2357;&#2367;&#2349;&#2366;&#2332;&#2367;&#2340; &#2325;&#2367;&#2351;&#2366; &#2332;&#2366;&#2340;&#2366; &#2361;&#2376;, &#2340;&#2379; &#2358;&#2375;&#2359; 48 &#2348;&#2330;&#2340;&#2366; &#2361;&#2376;, &#2324;&#2352; &#2319;&#2325; &#2309;&#2344;&#2381;&#2351; &#2360;&#2306;&#2326;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366; &#2325;&#2379; &#2313;&#2360;&#2368; &#2349;&#2366;&#2332;&#2325; &#2360;&#2375; &#2357;&#2367;&#2349;&#2366;&#2332;&#2367;&#2340; &#2325;&#2367;&#2351;&#2366; &#2332;&#2366;&#2340;&#2366; &#2361;&#2376;, &#2340;&#2379; &#2358;&#2375;&#2359; 33 &#2348;&#2330;&#2340;&#2366; &#2361;&#2376;&#2404; &#2351;&#2342;&#2367; &#2342;&#2379;&#2344;&#2379;&#2306; &#2360;&#2306;&#2326;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366;&#2323;&#2306; &#2325;&#2375; &#2351;&#2379;&#2327; &#2325;&#2379; &#2319;&#2325; &#2361;&#2368; &#2344;&#2367;&#2358;&#2381;&#2330;&#2367;&#2340; &#2349;&#2366;&#2332;&#2325; &#2360;&#2375; &#2357;&#2367;&#2349;&#2366;&#2332;&#2367;&#2340; &#2325;&#2367;&#2351;&#2366; &#2332;&#2366;&#2340;&#2366; &#2361;&#2376;, &#2340;&#2379; &#2358;&#2375;&#2359; 29 &#2348;&#2330;&#2340;&#2366; &#2361;&#2376;&#2404; &#2344;&#2367;&#2358;&#2381;&#2330;&#2367;&#2340; &#2349;&#2366;&#2332;&#2325; &#2332;&#2381;&#2334;&#2366;&#2340; &#2325;&#2368;&#2332;&#2367;&#2319;&#2404;</p>", "options_en": ["58", "52", "56", "54"], "options_hi": ["58", "52", "56", "54"], "answer": 1, "solution_en": "<p>N<sub>1</sub>/D = R<sub>1</sub>, N<sub>2</sub>/D = R<sub>2</sub>, (N<sub>1</sub> + N<sub>2</sub>)/D = R<sub>3</sub></p><p>D = R<sub>1</sub> + R<sub>2</sub>  -  R<sub>3</sub> = 48 + 33  -  29 = 52 </p>", "solution_hi": "<p>N<sub>1</sub>/D = R<sub>1</sub>, N<sub>2</sub>/D = R<sub>2</sub>, (N<sub>1</sub> + N<sub>2</sub>)/D = R<sub>3</sub></p><p>D = R<sub>1</sub> + R<sub>2</sub>  -  R<sub>3</sub> = 48 + 33  -  29 = 52 </p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25, "chap": "Number System"}, {"q_en": "<p>Last month, Anju's monthly saving was Rs. 2500 and Varun's monthly saving was Rs. 3200. This month, Anju's monthly saving is Rs 2900. and Varun's monthly saving is Rs. 3800. Find the value of [(Y  -  X) * 100/Y)], where X% is the percentage increase in Varun's monthly saving this month over last month and Y% is the percentage increase in Anju's monthly saving this month over last month.</p>", "q_hi": "<p>&#2346;&#2367;&#2331;&#2354;&#2375; &#2350;&#2361;&#2368;&#2344;&#2375;, &#2309;&#2306;&#2332;&#2370; &#2325;&#2368; &#2350;&#2366;&#2360;&#2367;&#2325; &#2348;&#2330;&#2340; 2500 &#2352;&#2369;&#2346;&#2351;&#2375; &#2341;&#2368; &#2324;&#2352; &#2357;&#2352;&#2369;&#2339; &#2325;&#2368; &#2350;&#2366;&#2360;&#2367;&#2325; &#2348;&#2330;&#2340; 3200 &#2352;&#2369;&#2346;&#2351;&#2375; &#2341;&#2368;&#2404; &#2311;&#2360; &#2350;&#2361;&#2368;&#2344;&#2375;, &#2309;&#2306;&#2332;&#2370; &#2325;&#2368; &#2350;&#2366;&#2360;&#2367;&#2325; &#2348;&#2330;&#2340; 2900 &#2352;&#2369;&#2346;&#2351;&#2375; &#2361;&#2376; &#2324;&#2352; &#2357;&#2352;&#2369;&#2339; &#2325;&#2368; &#2350;&#2366;&#2360;&#2367;&#2325; &#2348;&#2330;&#2340; 3800 &#2352;&#2369;&#2346;&#2351;&#2375; &#2361;&#2376;&#2404; [(Y - X) * 100/Y)] &#2325;&#2366; &#2350;&#2366;&#2344; &#2332;&#2381;&#2334;&#2366;&#2340; &#2325;&#2368;&#2332;&#2367;&#2319;, &#2332;&#2361;&#2366;&#2305; X% &#2346;&#2367;&#2331;&#2354;&#2375; &#2350;&#2361;&#2368;&#2344;&#2375; &#2325;&#2368; &#2340;&#2369;&#2354;&#2344;&#2366; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2311;&#2360; &#2350;&#2361;&#2368;&#2344;&#2375; &#2357;&#2352;&#2369;&#2339; &#2325;&#2368; &#2350;&#2366;&#2360;&#2367;&#2325; &#2348;&#2330;&#2340; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2346;&#2381;&#2352;&#2340;&#2367;&#2358;&#2340; &#2357;&#2371;&#2342;&#2381;&#2343;&#2367; &#2361;&#2376; &#2324;&#2352; Y% &#2346;&#2367;&#2331;&#2354;&#2375; &#2350;&#2361;&#2368;&#2344;&#2375; &#2325;&#2368; &#2340;&#2369;&#2354;&#2344;&#2366; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2311;&#2360; &#2350;&#2361;&#2368;&#2344;&#2375; &#2309;&#2306;&#2332;&#2370; &#2325;&#2368; &#2350;&#2366;&#2360;&#2367;&#2325; &#2348;&#2330;&#2340; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2346;&#2381;&#2352;&#2340;&#2367;&#2358;&#2340; &#2357;&#2371;&#2342;&#2381;&#2343;&#2367; &#2361;&#2376;&#2404;</p>", "options_en": ["17.1845", "17.1875", "17.1895", "17.1825"], "options_hi": ["17.1845", "17.1875", "17.1895", "17.1825"], "answer": 1, "solution_en": "<p>Anju's monthly saving last month = Rs. 2500</p><p>Anju's monthly saving this month = Rs. 2900</p><p>Y = (2900  -  2500) * 100/2500 = 16%</p><p>Varun's monthly saving last month = Rs. 3200</p><p>Varun's monthly saving this month = Rs. 3800</p><p>X = (3800  -  3200) * 100/3200 = 18.75</p><p>Hence, [(Y  -  X) * 100/Y] = [(18.75  -  16) * 100/16] = 17.1875</p>", "solution_hi": "<p>Anju's monthly saving last month = Rs. 2500</p><p>Anju's monthly saving this month = Rs. 2900</p><p>Y = (2900  -  2500) * 100/2500 = 16%</p><p>Varun's monthly saving last month = Rs. 3200</p><p>Varun's monthly saving this month = Rs. 3800</p><p>X = (3800  -  3200) * 100/3200 = 18.75</p><p>Hence, [(Y  -  X) * 100/Y] = [(18.75  -  16) * 100/16] = 17.1875</p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25, "chap": "Percentage"}, {"q_en": "<p><b>Directions: </b>Pie chart shows the distance travelled by a person by different vehicle in his journey as a per cent of total distance.</p><p><img width=382 height=336 id=\"Chart 1\" src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p3515/image001.png\"></p><p>Find the central angle made by 'the distance travelled by Auto' at the centre of pie chart:</p>", "q_hi": "<p><b>&#2344;&#2367;&#2352;&#2381;&#2342;&#2375;&#2358; : </b>&#2342;&#2367;&#2351;&#2366; &#2327;&#2351;&#2366; &#2357;&#2371;&#2340;&#2381;&#2340;&#2368;&#2351; &#2310;&#2352;&#2375;&#2326; &#2319;&#2325; &#2357;&#2381;&#2351;&#2325;&#2381;&#2340;&#2367; &#2342;&#2381;&#2357;&#2366;&#2352;&#2366; &#2309;&#2346;&#2344;&#2368; &#2351;&#2366;&#2340;&#2381;&#2352;&#2366; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2357;&#2367;&#2349;&#2367;&#2344;&#2381;&#2344; &#2357;&#2366;&#2361;&#2344;&#2379;&#2306; &#2342;&#2381;&#2357;&#2366;&#2352;&#2366; &#2340;&#2351; &#2325;&#2368; &#2327;&#2312; &#2342;&#2370;&#2352;&#2368; &#2325;&#2379; &#2325;&#2369;&#2354; &#2342;&#2370;&#2352;&#2368; &#2325;&#2375; &#2346;&#2381;&#2352;&#2340;&#2367;&#2358;&#2340; &#2325;&#2375; &#2352;&#2370;&#2346; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2342;&#2352;&#2381;&#2358;&#2366;&#2340;&#2366; &#2361;&#2376;&#2404;</p><p><img width=\"382\" height=\"336\" id=\"Chart 1\" src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p3515/image001.png\"></p><p>&#2357;&#2371;&#2340;&#2381;&#2340;&#2368;&#2351; &#2310;&#2352;&#2375;&#2326; &#2325;&#2375; &#2325;&#2375;&#2306;&#2342;&#2381;&#2352; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; '&#2321;&#2335;&#2379; &#2342;&#2381;&#2357;&#2366;&#2352;&#2366; &#2340;&#2351; &#2325;&#2368; &#2327;&#2312; &#2342;&#2370;&#2352;&#2368;' &#2342;&#2381;&#2357;&#2366;&#2352;&#2366; &#2348;&#2344;&#2344;&#2375; &#2357;&#2366;&#2354;&#2366; &#2325;&#2375;&#2306;&#2342;&#2381;&#2352;&#2368;&#2351; &#2325;&#2379;&#2339; &#2332;&#2381;&#2334;&#2366;&#2340; &#2325;&#2368;&#2332;&#2367;&#2319;&#2404;</p>", "options_en": ["64.8&deg;", "54&deg;", "64&deg;", "43.2&deg;"], "options_hi": ["64.8<sup>0</sup>", "54<sup>0</sup>", "64<sup>0</sup>", "43.2<sup>0</sup>"], "answer": 1, "solution_en": "<p>Required angle = (15/100) * 360 = 54&deg;</p>", "solution_hi": "<p>Required angle = (15/100) * 360 = 54&deg;</p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25, "chap": "Percentage"}, {"q_en": "<p>A boat can cover a distance of 96 km in downstream and after reaching to destination it again returns to mid-point in total of 7 hours. The speed of the stream is 5/16 times of the downstream speed of the boat, then in how much time it will cover 84 km in upstream?</p>", "q_hi": "<p>&#2319;&#2325; &#2344;&#2366;&#2357; &#2343;&#2366;&#2352;&#2366; &#2325;&#2375; &#2309;&#2344;&#2369;&#2325;&#2370;&#2354; 96 km &#2325;&#2368; &#2342;&#2370;&#2352;&#2368; &#2340;&#2351; &#2325;&#2352; &#2360;&#2325;&#2340;&#2368; &#2361;&#2376; &#2324;&#2352; &#2327;&#2306;&#2340;&#2357;&#2381;&#2351; &#2340;&#2325; &#2346;&#2361;&#2369;&#2306;&#2330;&#2344;&#2375; &#2325;&#2375; &#2348;&#2366;&#2342; &#2351;&#2361; &#2325;&#2369;&#2354; 7 &#2328;&#2306;&#2335;&#2375; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2347;&#2367;&#2352; &#2360;&#2375; &#2350;&#2343;&#2381;&#2351; &#2348;&#2367;&#2306;&#2342;&#2369; &#2346;&#2352; &#2354;&#2380;&#2335; &#2310;&#2340;&#2368; &#2361;&#2376;&#2404; &#2343;&#2366;&#2352;&#2366; &#2325;&#2368; &#2330;&#2366;&#2354;, &#2344;&#2366;&#2357; &#2325;&#2368; &#2343;&#2366;&#2352;&#2366; &#2325;&#2375; &#2309;&#2344;&#2369;&#2325;&#2370;&#2354; &#2330;&#2366;&#2354; &#2325;&#2368; 5/16 &#2327;&#2369;&#2344;&#2366; &#2361;&#2376;, &#2340;&#2379; &#2351;&#2361; &#2343;&#2366;&#2352;&#2366; &#2325;&#2375; &#2346;&#2381;&#2352;&#2340;&#2367;&#2325;&#2370;&#2354; 84 km &#2325;&#2368; &#2342;&#2370;&#2352;&#2368; &#2325;&#2367;&#2340;&#2344;&#2375; &#2360;&#2350;&#2351; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2340;&#2351; &#2325;&#2352;&#2375;&#2327;&#2368;?</p>", "options_en": ["9 hours", "6 hours", "7 hours", "4 hours"], "options_hi": ["9 &#2328;&#2306;&#2335;&#2375;", "6 &#2328;&#2306;&#2335;&#2375;", "7 &#2328;&#2306;&#2335;&#2375;", "4 &#2328;&#2306;&#2335;&#2375;"], "answer": 2, "solution_en": "<p>Let speed of the stream = 5x km/h and downstream speed of the boat = 16x km/h</p><p>So, speed of boat in still water = 16x  -  5x = 11x km/h and upstream speed of the boat = 11x  -  5x = 6x km/h</p><p>According to the question,</p><p>96/16x + 48/6x = 7</p><p>=&gt; x = 2 km/h</p><p>Required time = 84/(2 * 6) = 7 hours</p>", "solution_hi": "<p>Let speed of the stream = 5x km/h and downstream speed of the boat = 16x km/h</p><p>So, speed of boat in still water = 16x  -  5x = 11x km/h and upstream speed of the boat = 11x  -  5x = 6x km/h</p><p>According to the question,</p><p>96/16x + 48/6x = 7</p><p>=&gt; x = 2 km/h</p><p>Required time = 84/(2 * 6) = 7 hours</p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25, "chap": "Time, Speed & Distance"}, {"q_en": "<p>If a number is doubled and 15 is added to it, and the resultant is squared, then the final value will be 1681. What is that number?</p>", "q_hi": "<p>&#2351;&#2342;&#2367; &#2325;&#2367;&#2360;&#2368; &#2360;&#2306;&#2326;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366; &#2325;&#2379; &#2342;&#2379;&#2327;&#2369;&#2344;&#2366; &#2325;&#2352; &#2342;&#2367;&#2351;&#2366; &#2332;&#2366;&#2319; &#2324;&#2352; &#2313;&#2360;&#2350;&#2375;&#2306; 15 &#2332;&#2379;&#2337;&#2364; &#2342;&#2367;&#2351;&#2366; &#2332;&#2366;&#2319;, &#2340;&#2341;&#2366; &#2346;&#2352;&#2367;&#2339;&#2366;&#2350;&#2368; &#2360;&#2306;&#2326;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366; &#2325;&#2366; &#2357;&#2352;&#2381;&#2327; &#2325;&#2352; &#2342;&#2367;&#2351;&#2366; &#2332;&#2366;&#2319;, &#2340;&#2379; &#2309;&#2306;&#2340;&#2367;&#2350; &#2350;&#2366;&#2344; 1681 &#2361;&#2379;&#2327;&#2366;&#2404; &#2357;&#2361; &#2360;&#2306;&#2326;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366; &#2325;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366; &#2361;&#2376;?</p>", "options_en": ["12", "14", "11", "13"], "options_hi": ["12", "14", "11", "13"], "answer": 3, "solution_en": "<p>Let the number be a</p><p>(a * 2 + 15)<sup>2</sup> = 1681</p><p>=> 2a + 15 = 41</p><p>=> 2a = 26</p><p>=> a = 13</p>", "solution_hi": "<p>Let the number be a</p><p>(a * 2 + 15)<sup>2</sup> = 1681</p><p>=> 2a + 15 = 41</p><p>=> 2a = 26</p><p>=> a = 13</p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25, "chap": "Mensuration (2D)"}, {"q_en": "<p>Which of the following is a perfect cube?</p>", "q_hi": "<p>&#2351;&#2342;&#2367; a &#2324;&#2352; b &#2360;&#2350; &#2315;&#2339;&#2366;&#2340;&#2381;&#2350;&#2325; &#2360;&#2306;&#2326;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366;&#2319;&#2305; &#2361;&#2376;&#2306;, &#2340;&#2379; &#2344;&#2367;&#2350;&#2381;&#2344;&#2354;&#2367;&#2326;&#2367;&#2340; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2360;&#2375; &#2325;&#2380;&#2344; &#2360;&#2368; &#2357;&#2367;&#2359;&#2350; &#2343;&#2344;&#2366;&#2340;&#2381;&#2350;&#2325; &#2360;&#2306;&#2326;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366; &#2361;&#2376;?</p>", "options_en": ["1000000", "2160000", "194000", "12500000"], "options_hi": ["ab + 1", "ab  -  2", "a + b", "2(a + b)"], "answer": 2, "solution_en": "<p>Prime numbers between 70 and 85 = 71, 73, 79, 83</p><p>Required sum = 71 + 73 + 79 + 83 = 306</p>", "solution_hi": "<p>Prime numbers between 70 and 85 = 71, 73, 79, 83</p><p>Required sum = 71 + 73 + 79 + 83 = 306</p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25, "chap": "Number System"}, {"q_en": "<p>Varun and Sandeep started for a car race from the same point, in the same direction and at the same time on a circular track of length 1635 m with the speeds of 90 km/h and 108 km/h, respectively. After how much time (in seconds) will they meet again for the first time?</p><p>Options:</p>", "q_hi": "&#2357;&#2352;&#2369;&#2339; &#2324;&#2352; &#2360;&#2306;&#2342;&#2368;&#2346; &#2319;&#2325; &#2361;&#2368; &#2360;&#2381;&#2341;&#2366;&#2344; &#2360;&#2375;, &#2319;&#2325; &#2361;&#2368; &#2342;&#2367;&#2358;&#2366; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2324;&#2352; &#2319;&#2325; &#2361;&#2368; &#2360;&#2350;&#2351; &#2346;&#2352; 1635 &#2350;&#2368;&#2335;&#2352; &#2354;&#2306;&#2348;&#2375; &#2319;&#2325; &#2357;&#2371;&#2340;&#2381;&#2340;&#2366;&#2325;&#2366;&#2352; &#2335;&#2381;&#2352;&#2376;&#2325; &#2346;&#2352; &#2325;&#2381;&#2352;&#2350;&#2358;&#2307; 90 &#2325;&#2367;&#2350;&#2368;/&#2328;&#2306;&#2335;&#2366; &#2324;&#2352; 108 &#2325;&#2367;&#2350;&#2368;/&#2328;&#2306;&#2335;&#2366; &#2325;&#2368; &#2327;&#2340;&#2367; &#2360;&#2375; &#2325;&#2366;&#2352; &#2352;&#2375;&#2360; &#2325;&#2375; &#2354;&#2367;&#2319; &#2344;&#2367;&#2325;&#2354;&#2375;&#2404; &#2325;&#2367;&#2340;&#2344;&#2375; &#2360;&#2350;&#2351; (&#2360;&#2375;&#2325;&#2306;&#2337; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306;) &#2325;&#2375; &#2348;&#2366;&#2342; &#2357;&#2375; &#2346;&#2361;&#2354;&#2368; &#2348;&#2366;&#2352; &#2347;&#2367;&#2352; &#2360;&#2375; &#2350;&#2367;&#2354;&#2375;&#2306;&#2327;&#2375;?</p><p>&#2357;&#2367;&#2325;&#2354;&#2381;&#2346;:", "options_en": ["324", "325", "327", "326"], "options_hi": ["324", "325", "327", "326"], "answer": 2, "solution_en": "<p>Step 1: Calculate their relative speed.</p><p>&#183; Speed of Varun = 90&#8201;km/h = 90  X 5/18 = 25&#8201;m/s</p><p>&#183; Speed of Sandeep = 108&#8201;km/h = 108  X 5/18 = 30&#8201;m/s</p><p>&#183; Relative speed = 30  -  25 = 5&#8201;m/s</p><p>Step 2: Time to meet again.</p><p>&#183; They meet when the relative distance travelled equals the length of the track.</p><p>Time = Track Length/Relative Speed = 1,635/5 = 327&#8201;seconds</p><p>Thus, they will meet again after 327 seconds.</p>", "solution_hi": "<p>Step 1: Calculate their relative speed.</p><p>&#183; Speed of Varun = 90&#8201;km/h = 90  X 5/18 = 25&#8201;m/s</p><p>&#183; Speed of Sandeep = 108&#8201;km/h = 108  X 5/18 = 30&#8201;m/s</p><p>&#183; Relative speed = 30  -  25 = 5&#8201;m/s</p><p>Step 2: Time to meet again.</p><p>&#183; They meet when the relative distance travelled equals the length of the track.</p><p>Time = Track Length/Relative Speed = 1,635/5 = 327&#8201;seconds</p><p>Thus, they will meet again after 327 seconds.</p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25, "chap": "Time, Speed & Distance"}, {"q_en": "<p><div>&nbsp;If X =&nbsp;<div style=\"display: inline-block;position: relative;vertical-align: middle;\"><span style=\"text-align:center;display: block; padding: 0;\">15", "q_hi": "<p><div>&#2351;&#2342;&#2367; X = <div style=\"display: inline-block;position: relative;vertical-align: middle;\"><span style=\"text-align:center;display: block; padding: 0;\">15", "options_en": ["159", "129", "139", "141"], "options_hi": ["159", "129", "139", "141"], "answer": 2, "solution_en": "<p><img width=160 height=37 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p23849/image037.png\"></p><p><img width=108 height=37 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p23849/image039.png\"></p><p><img width=116 height=37 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p23849/image040.png\"></p><p><img width=160 height=17 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p23849/image041.png\"></p><p><img width=87 height=17 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p23849/image042.png\"></p><p><img width=55 height=17 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p23849/image043.png\"></p><p><img width=168 height=19 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p23849/image044.png\"></p>", "solution_hi": "<p><img width=160 height=37 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p23849/image037.png\"></p><p><img width=108 height=37 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p23849/image039.png\"></p><p><img width=116 height=37 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p23849/image040.png\"></p><p><img width=160 height=17 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p23849/image041.png\"></p><p><img width=87 height=17 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p23849/image042.png\"></p><p><img width=55 height=17 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p23849/image043.png\"></p><p><img width=168 height=19 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p23849/image044.png\"></p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25, "chap": "Percentage"}, {"q_en": "<p>Rational number that lies between (12/7) and (16/5)</p>", "q_hi": "<p>(12/7) &#2324;&#2352; (16/5) &#2325;&#2375; &#2348;&#2368;&#2330; &#2360;&#2381;&#2341;&#2367;&#2340; &#2346;&#2352;&#2367;&#2350;&#2375;&#2351; &#2360;&#2306;&#2326;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366; &#2361;&#2376;:</p>", "options_en": ["14/3", "19/14", "17/6", "13/4"], "options_hi": ["14/3", "19/14", "17/6", "13/4"], "answer": 2, "solution_en": "<p>According to the Question,</p><p>12/7 = 1.71 and 16/5 = 3.20</p><p>From options a) 14/3 =4.67</p><p>b) 19/14 =1.36</p><p>c) 17/6 =2.83</p><p>d) 13/4 =3.25</p><p>So, the rational number that lie between the above fractions is:</p><p>17/6 = 2.83 Ans.</p>", "solution_hi": "<p>According to the Question,</p><p>12/7 = 1.71 and 16/5 = 3.20</p><p>From options a) 14/3 =4.67</p><p>b) 19/14 =1.36</p><p>c) 17/6 =2.83</p><p>d) 13/4 =3.25</p><p>So, the rational number that lie between the above fractions is:</p><p>17/6 = 2.83 Ans.</p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25, "chap": "Number System"}, {"q_en": "<p>The half of the length of the common chord of two intersecting circles is 16 cm. If the radii of the circles are 8&radic;5 cm and 20 cm, then the distance between the centres (in cm) is:</p>", "q_hi": "<p>&#2342;&#2379; &#2346;&#2381;&#2352;&#2340;&#2367;&#2330;&#2381;&#2331;&#2375;&#2342;&#2368; &#2357;&#2371;&#2340;&#2381;&#2340;&#2379;&#2306; &#2325;&#2368; &#2313;&#2349;&#2351;&#2344;&#2367;&#2359;&#2381;&#2336; &#2332;&#2368;&#2357;&#2366; &#2325;&#2368; &#2354;&#2306;&#2348;&#2366;&#2312; &#2325;&#2366; &#2310;&#2343;&#2366; 16 &#2360;&#2375;&#2350;&#2368; &#2361;&#2376;&#2404; &#2351;&#2342;&#2367; &#2357;&#2371;&#2340;&#2381;&#2340;&#2379;&#2306; &#2325;&#2368; &#2340;&#2381;&#2352;&#2367;&#2332;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366;&#2319;&#2305; 8&radic;5 &#2360;&#2375;&#2350;&#2368; &#2324;&#2352; 20 &#2360;&#2375;&#2350;&#2368; &#2361;&#2376;&#2306;, &#2340;&#2379; &#2325;&#2375;&#2344;&#2381;&#2342;&#2381;&#2352;&#2379;&#2306; &#2325;&#2375; &#2348;&#2368;&#2330; &#2325;&#2368; &#2342;&#2370;&#2352;&#2368; (&#2360;&#2375;&#2350;&#2368; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306;) &#2361;&#2376;:</p>", "options_en": ["20 cm", "18 cm", "24 cm", "16 cm"], "options_hi": ["20 cm", "18 cm", "24 cm", "16 cm"], "answer": 0, "solution_en": "<p><img width=199 height=129 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p23304/image032.png\"></p><p>Given that MN = 16 cm, AM = 8&radic;5 cm, and BM = 20 cm</p><p>In &#916; AMN,</p><p><img width=132 height=36 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p23304/image033.png\"></p><p><img width=117 height=21 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p23304/image034.png\"></p><p><img width=115 height=21 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p23304/image035.png\"></p><p>In &#916; BMN,</p><p><img width=121 height=31 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p23304/image036.png\"></p><p><img width=117 height=21 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p23304/image037.png\"></p><p><img width=129 height=21 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p23304/image038.png\"></p><p><img width=288 height=17 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p23304/image039.png\"></p>", "solution_hi": "<p><img width=199 height=129 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p23304/image032.png\"></p><p>Given that MN = 16 cm, AM = 8&radic;5 cm, and BM = 20 cm</p><p>In &#916; AMN,</p><p><img width=132 height=36 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p23304/image033.png\"></p><p><img width=117 height=21 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p23304/image034.png\"></p><p><img width=115 height=21 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p23304/image035.png\"></p><p>In &#916; BMN,</p><p><img width=121 height=31 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p23304/image036.png\"></p><p><img width=117 height=21 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p23304/image037.png\"></p><p><img width=129 height=21 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p23304/image038.png\"></p><p><img width=288 height=17 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p23304/image039.png\"></p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25, "chap": "Mensuration (2D)"}, {"q_en": "<p>A polygon has 945 diagonals. The no. of sides of the polygon are  -</p>", "q_hi": "<p>&#2319;&#2325; &#2348;&#2361;&#2369;&#2349;&#2369;&#2332; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; 945 &#2357;&#2367;&#2325;&#2352;&#2381;&#2339; &#2361;&#2376;&#2306;&#2404; &#2348;&#2361;&#2369;&#2349;&#2369;&#2332; &#2325;&#2368; &#2349;&#2369;&#2332;&#2366;&#2323;&#2306; &#2325;&#2368; &#2360;&#2306;&#2326;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366; &#2361;&#2376; -</p>", "options_en": ["45", "55", "25", "35"], "options_hi": ["45", "55", "25", "35"], "answer": 0, "solution_en": "<p>The no. of diagonals in a polygon = n(n-3)/2 (where, n = number of sides)</p><p>945 = n(n-3)/2</p><p>1890 = n<sup>2</sup>  -  3n</p><p>n<sup>2</sup>  -  3n  -  1890 = 0</p><p>(n  -  45)(n + 42) = 0</p><p>n = 45,  -  42</p><p>(Number of sides cannot be negative.)</p><p>\\ n = 45</p>", "solution_hi": "<p>The no. of diagonals in a polygon = n(n-3)/2 (where, n = number of sides)</p><p>945 = n(n-3)/2</p><p>1890 = n<sup>2</sup>  -  3n</p><p>n<sup>2</sup>  -  3n  -  1890 = 0</p><p>(n  -  45)(n + 42) = 0</p><p>n = 45,  -  42</p><p>(Number of sides cannot be negative.)</p><p>\\ n = 45</p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25, "chap": "Mensuration (2D)"}, {"q_en": "<p>The given pie chart shows the annual agricultural production (in tonnes) in a region. The total production is 8600 tonnes.</p><p>What is the annual production of rice in the region?</p><p><img width=318 height=240 id=\"Picture 23\" src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p27092/image022.png\"></p>", "q_hi": "&#2342;&#2367;&#2351;&#2366; &#2327;&#2351;&#2366; &#2346;&#2366;&#2312; &#2330;&#2366;&#2352;&#2381;&#2335; &#2319;&#2325; &#2325;&#2381;&#2359;&#2375;&#2340;&#2381;&#2352; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2357;&#2366;&#2352;&#2381;&#2359;&#2367;&#2325; &#2325;&#2371;&#2359;&#2367; &#2313;&#2340;&#2381;&#2346;&#2366;&#2342;&#2344; (&#2335;&#2344; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306;) &#2342;&#2352;&#2381;&#2358;&#2366;&#2340;&#2366; &#2361;&#2376;&#2404; &#2325;&#2369;&#2354; &#2313;&#2340;&#2381;&#2346;&#2366;&#2342;&#2344; 8600 &#2335;&#2344; &#2361;&#2376;&#2404;</p><p>&#2325;&#2381;&#2359;&#2375;&#2340;&#2381;&#2352; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2330;&#2366;&#2357;&#2354; &#2325;&#2366; &#2357;&#2366;&#2352;&#2381;&#2359;&#2367;&#2325; &#2313;&#2340;&#2381;&#2346;&#2366;&#2342;&#2344; &#2325;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366; &#2361;&#2376;?</p><p><img width=318 height=240 id=\"Picture 23\" src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p27092/image022.png\">", "options_en": ["5012 tonnes", "1052 tonnes", "2150 tonnes", "2051 tonnes"], "options_hi": ["5012 &#2335;&#2344;", "1052 &#2335;&#2344;", "2150 &#2335;&#2344;", "2051 &#2335;&#2344;"], "answer": 2, "solution_en": "<p>Production of rice = (25 / 100)  X  8600</p><p>= 0.25  X  8600</p><p>= 2150 tonnes</p>", "solution_hi": "<p>Production of rice = (25 / 100)  X  8600</p><p>= 0.25  X  8600</p><p>= 2150 tonnes</p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25, "chap": "Percentage"}, {"q_en": "<p>What least number should be added to 16000 to make it a perfect square?</p>", "q_hi": "<p>16000 &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2325;&#2380;&#2344; &#2360;&#2368; &#2331;&#2379;&#2335;&#2368; &#2360;&#2375; &#2331;&#2379;&#2335;&#2368; &#2360;&#2306;&#2326;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366; &#2332;&#2379;&#2337;&#2364;&#2368; &#2332;&#2366;&#2319; &#2325;&#2367; &#2357;&#2361; &#2346;&#2370;&#2352;&#2381;&#2339; &#2357;&#2352;&#2381;&#2327; &#2348;&#2344; &#2332;&#2366;&#2319;?</p>", "options_en": ["127", "128", "129", "130"], "options_hi": ["127", "128", "129", "130"], "answer": 2, "solution_en": "<p>(127)<sup>2</sup> = 16129</p><p>Least number that should be added = 16129  -  16000 = 129</p>", "solution_hi": "<p>(127)<sup>2</sup> = 16129</p><p>Least number that should be added = 16129  -  16000 = 129</p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25, "chap": "Number System"}, {"q_en": "<p>In a 2400 m race, bike A beats bike B by 300 m. Bike B beats bike C by 200 m in an 1800 m race. If bike A beats bike C by 20 seconds in a 1440 m race, then what is the speed of bike C? </p>", "q_hi": "<p>2400 &#2350;&#2368;&#2335;&#2352; &#2325;&#2368; &#2342;&#2380;&#2337;&#2364; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306;, &#2348;&#2366;&#2311;&#2325; A, &#2348;&#2366;&#2311;&#2325; B &#2360;&#2375; 300 &#2350;&#2368;&#2335;&#2352; &#2310;&#2327;&#2375; &#2361;&#2376;&#2404; 1800 &#2350;&#2368;&#2335;&#2352; &#2325;&#2368; &#2342;&#2380;&#2337;&#2364; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2348;&#2366;&#2311;&#2325; B, &#2348;&#2366;&#2311;&#2325; C &#2360;&#2375; 200 &#2350;&#2368;&#2335;&#2352; &#2310;&#2327;&#2375; &#2361;&#2376;&#2404; &#2351;&#2342;&#2367; 1440 &#2350;&#2368;&#2335;&#2352; &#2325;&#2368; &#2342;&#2380;&#2337;&#2364; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2348;&#2366;&#2311;&#2325; A, &#2348;&#2366;&#2311;&#2325; C &#2360;&#2375; 20 &#2360;&#2375;&#2325;&#2306;&#2337; &#2310;&#2327;&#2375; &#2361;&#2376;, &#2340;&#2379; &#2348;&#2366;&#2311;&#2325; C &#2325;&#2368; &#2327;&#2340;&#2367; &#2325;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366; &#2361;&#2376;? </p>", "options_en": ["16 m/sec", "19 m/sec", "15 m/sec", "18 m/sec"], "options_hi": ["16 &#2350;&#2368;&#2335;&#2352;/&#2360;&#2375;&#2325;&#2306;&#2337;", "19 &#2350;&#2368;&#2335;&#2352;/&#2360;&#2375;&#2325;&#2306;&#2337;", "15 &#2350;&#2368;&#2335;&#2352;/&#2360;&#2375;&#2325;&#2306;&#2337;", "18 &#2350;&#2368;&#2335;&#2352;/&#2360;&#2375;&#2325;&#2306;&#2337;"], "answer": 0, "solution_en": "<p>When bike A covers 2400 m bike B covers 2100 m</p><p>The ratio of speed = 8: 7 </p><p>When bike B covers 1800 m bike C covers 1600 m</p><p>The ratio of speed = 9: 8</p><p>The ratio of speed of A, B, and C = 72:63:56 </p><p>When bike A covers 1440 m, C covers = 1440 * 56/72 = 1120 m</p><p>So, difference = 1440  -  1120 = 320 m</p><p>Bike C will cover the remaining 320 m in 20 seconds </p><p>Hence, the speed of bike C = 320/20 = 16 m/sec </p>", "solution_hi": "<p>When bike A covers 2400 m bike B covers 2100 m</p><p>The ratio of speed = 8: 7 </p><p>When bike B covers 1800 m bike C covers 1600 m</p><p>The ratio of speed = 9: 8</p><p>The ratio of speed of A, B, and C = 72:63:56 </p><p>When bike A covers 1440 m, C covers = 1440 * 56/72 = 1120 m</p><p>So, difference = 1440  -  1120 = 320 m</p><p>Bike C will cover the remaining 320 m in 20 seconds </p><p>Hence, the speed of bike C = 320/20 = 16 m/sec </p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25, "chap": "Time, Speed & Distance"}, {"q_en": "<p>The perimeter of an isosceles triangle is 50 cm. If the base is 18 cm, then find the length of each of the equal sides.</p>", "q_hi": "<p>&#2319;&#2325; &#2360;&#2350;&#2342;&#2381;&#2357;&#2367;&#2348;&#2366;&#2361;&#2369; &#2340;&#2381;&#2352;&#2367;&#2349;&#2369;&#2332; &#2325;&#2366; &#2346;&#2352;&#2367;&#2350;&#2366;&#2346; 50 cm &#2361;&#2376;&#2404; &#2351;&#2342;&#2367; &#2311;&#2360;&#2325;&#2366; &#2310;&#2343;&#2366;&#2352; 18 cm &#2361;&#2376;, &#2340;&#2379; &#2346;&#2381;&#2352;&#2340;&#2381;&#2351;&#2375;&#2325; &#2360;&#2350;&#2366;&#2344; &#2349;&#2369;&#2332;&#2366; &#2325;&#2368; &#2354;&#2306;&#2348;&#2366;&#2312; &#2332;&#2381;&#2334;&#2366;&#2340; &#2325;&#2368;&#2332;&#2367;&#2319;&#2404;</p>", "options_en": ["18 cm", "25 cm", "16 cm", "32 cm"], "options_hi": ["18 cm", "25 cm", "16 cm", "32 cm"], "answer": 2, "solution_en": "<p>Let the length of each of the equal sides = X cm</p><p>Perimeter = 50 cm</p><p>X + X + 18 = 50</p><p>2X = 32</p><p>X = 16.</p>", "solution_hi": "<p>Let the length of each of the equal sides = X cm</p><p>Perimeter = 50 cm</p><p>X + X + 18 = 50</p><p>2X = 32</p><p>X = 16.</p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25, "chap": "Mensuration (2D)"}, {"q_en": "<p>Two trains started from a station, at the same time in the same direction, at speeds of 72 kmph and 60 kmph. What will be the distance between the two trains after 7 hours?</p>", "q_hi": "<p>&#2342;&#2379; &#2335;&#2381;&#2352;&#2375;&#2344;&#2375;&#2306; &#2319;&#2325; &#2361;&#2368; &#2360;&#2350;&#2351; &#2346;&#2352; &#2319;&#2325; &#2361;&#2368; &#2342;&#2367;&#2358;&#2366; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; 72 &#2325;&#2367;&#2350;&#2368; &#2346;&#2381;&#2352;&#2340;&#2367; &#2328;&#2306;&#2335;&#2375; &#2324;&#2352; 60 &#2325;&#2367;&#2350;&#2368; &#2346;&#2381;&#2352;&#2340;&#2367; &#2328;&#2306;&#2335;&#2375; &#2325;&#2368; &#2327;&#2340;&#2367; &#2360;&#2375; &#2319;&#2325; &#2360;&#2381;&#2335;&#2375;&#2358;&#2344; &#2360;&#2375; &#2330;&#2354; &#2352;&#2361;&#2368; &#2361;&#2376;&#2306;&#2404; 7 &#2328;&#2306;&#2335;&#2375; &#2348;&#2366;&#2342; &#2342;&#2379;&#2344;&#2379;&#2306; &#2335;&#2381;&#2352;&#2375;&#2344;&#2379;&#2306; &#2325;&#2375; &#2348;&#2368;&#2330; &#2325;&#2368; &#2342;&#2370;&#2352;&#2368; &#2325;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366; &#2361;&#2379;&#2327;&#2368;?</p>", "options_en": ["42 km", "50.4 km", "63 km", "84 km"], "options_hi": ["42 &#2325;&#2367;&#2350;&#2368;", "50.4 &#2325;&#2367;&#2350;&#2368;", "63 &#2325;&#2367;&#2350;&#2368;", "84 &#2325;&#2367;&#2350;&#2368;"], "answer": 3, "solution_en": "<p>Distance between them after one hour = 72  -  60 = 12km.</p><p>Therefore distance between them after 7 hours 12 x 7 = 84 km.</p><p></p>", "solution_hi": "<p>Distance between them after one hour = 72  -  60 = 12km.</p><p>Therefore distance between them after 7 hours 12 x 7 = 84 km.</p><p></p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25, "chap": "Time, Speed & Distance"}, {"q_en": "<p>Fresh and dry orange contains 78% and 36% water. Find the quantity of dry fruit can be obtained from 800 kg of fresh orange.</p>", "q_hi": "<p>&#2340;&#2366;&#2332;&#2364;&#2375; &#2324;&#2352; &#2360;&#2370;&#2326;&#2375; &#2360;&#2306;&#2340;&#2352;&#2375; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; 78% &#2324;&#2352; 36% &#2346;&#2366;&#2344;&#2368; &#2361;&#2379;&#2340;&#2366; &#2361;&#2376;&#2404; 800 &#2325;&#2367;&#2354;&#2379;&#2327;&#2381;&#2352;&#2366;&#2350; &#2340;&#2366;&#2332;&#2375; &#2360;&#2306;&#2340;&#2352;&#2375; &#2360;&#2375; &#2346;&#2381;&#2352;&#2366;&#2346;&#2381;&#2340; &#2361;&#2379;&#2344;&#2375; &#2357;&#2366;&#2354;&#2375; &#2360;&#2370;&#2326;&#2375; &#2350;&#2375;&#2357;&#2375; &#2325;&#2368; &#2350;&#2366;&#2340;&#2381;&#2352;&#2366; &#2332;&#2381;&#2334;&#2366;&#2340; &#2325;&#2368;&#2332;&#2367;&#2319;&#2404;</p>", "options_en": ["290 kg", "285 kg", "280 kg", "275 kg"], "options_hi": ["290 &#2325;&#2367;&#2354;&#2379;&#2327;&#2381;&#2352;&#2366;&#2350;", "285 &#2325;&#2367;&#2354;&#2379;&#2327;&#2381;&#2352;&#2366;&#2350;", "280 &#2325;&#2367;&#2354;&#2379;&#2327;&#2381;&#2352;&#2366;&#2350;", "275 &#2325;&#2367;&#2354;&#2379;&#2327;&#2381;&#2352;&#2366;&#2350;"], "answer": 3, "solution_en": "<p>Pulp content in both the fresh fruit and dry fruit is same </p><p>Let weight of dry fruit be x kg </p><p>Fresh fruit 78% water and 22% pulp</p><p>Dry fruit 36% water and 64% pulp</p><p>22% of 800 = 64% of x</p><p>x = (22 * 800)/64 = 275 kg</p>", "solution_hi": "<p>Pulp content in both the fresh fruit and dry fruit is same </p><p>Let weight of dry fruit be x kg </p><p>Fresh fruit 78% water and 22% pulp</p><p>Dry fruit 36% water and 64% pulp</p><p>22% of 800 = 64% of x</p><p>x = (22 * 800)/64 = 275 kg</p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25, "chap": "Percentage"}, {"q_en": "<p>Find the sum of the greatest and smallest four  -  digit numbers that begins with 4 and ends with 2.</p>", "q_hi": "<p>1 &#2360;&#2375; 15 &#2340;&#2325; &#2309;&#2349;&#2366;&#2332;&#2381;&#2351; &#2360;&#2306;&#2326;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366;&#2323;&#2306; &#2325;&#2366; &#2327;&#2369;&#2339;&#2344;&#2347;&#2354; &#2361;&#2376; - </p>", "options_en": ["8844", "9044", "9124", "8994"], "options_hi": ["30030", "28760", "32480", "25410"], "answer": 0, "solution_en": "<p>All positive multiples of 8 less than 45 = 8, 16, 24, 32, 40</p><p>Product = 8 * 16 * 24 * 32 * 40 = 8<sup>6</sup> * 15</p><p>Required value = &#8731;(8<sup>6</sup> * 15) = 64&#8731;15</p>", "solution_hi": "<p>All positive multiples of 8 less than 45 = 8, 16, 24, 32, 40</p><p>Product = 8 * 16 * 24 * 32 * 40 = 8<sup>6</sup> * 15</p><p>Required value = &#8731;(8<sup>6</sup> * 15) = 64&#8731;15</p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25, "chap": "Number System"}, {"q_en": "<p>Which of the following fractions is smaller than 11/15 and greater 13/28 than?</p>", "q_hi": "<p>7.32<span style=\"text-decoration:overline\">8", "options_en": ["4/5", "9/16", "15/19", "16/35"], "options_hi": ["1649/450", "1649/225", "1657/225", "1657/450"], "answer": 1, "solution_en": "<p>11/15 = 0.733, 13/28 = 0.46</p><p>(a) 4/5 = 0.8 &gt; 0.733</p><p>(b) 9/16 = 0.5625, 0.733 &gt; 0.5625 &gt; 0.46 [satisfied]</p><p>(c) 15/19 = 0.789 &gt; 0.733</p><p>(d) 16/35 = 0.45 &lt; 0.46</p>", "solution_hi": "<p>11/15 = 0.733, 13/28 = 0.46</p><p>(a) 4/5 = 0.8 &gt; 0.733</p><p>(b) 9/16 = 0.5625, 0.733 &gt; 0.5625 &gt; 0.46 [satisfied]</p><p>(c) 15/19 = 0.789 &gt; 0.733</p><p>(d) 16/35 = 0.45 &lt; 0.46</p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25, "chap": "Number System"}, {"q_en": "<p>Aarav owns a watch worth &#8377;10,000. He sells it to Bhavin at a profit of 15%. After some days, Bhavin sells it back to Aarav at 15% loss. Find the percentage profit or loss faced by Aarav.</p>", "q_hi": "<p>&#2310;&#2352;&#2357; &#2325;&#2375; &#2346;&#2366;&#2360; 10,000 &#2337;&#2377;&#2354;&#2352; &#2325;&#2368; &#2325;&#2368;&#2350;&#2340; &#2325;&#2368; &#2319;&#2325; &#2328;&#2337;&#2364;&#2368; &#2361;&#2376;&#2404; &#2357;&#2361; &#2311;&#2360;&#2375; &#2349;&#2366;&#2357;&#2367;&#2344; &#2325;&#2379; 15% &#2354;&#2366;&#2349; &#2346;&#2352; &#2348;&#2375;&#2330;&#2340;&#2366; &#2361;&#2376;&#2404; &#2325;&#2369;&#2331; &#2342;&#2367;&#2344;&#2379;&#2306; &#2348;&#2366;&#2342; &#2349;&#2366;&#2357;&#2367;&#2344; &#2311;&#2360;&#2375; &#2357;&#2366;&#2346;&#2360; &#2310;&#2352;&#2357; &#2325;&#2379; 15% &#2361;&#2366;&#2344;&#2367; &#2346;&#2352; &#2348;&#2375;&#2330; &#2342;&#2375;&#2340;&#2366; &#2361;&#2376;&#2404; &#2310;&#2352;&#2357; &#2325;&#2379; &#2325;&#2367;&#2340;&#2344;&#2366; &#2346;&#2381;&#2352;&#2340;&#2367;&#2358;&#2340; &#2354;&#2366;&#2349; &#2351;&#2366; &#2361;&#2366;&#2344;&#2367; &#2361;&#2369;&#2312;, &#2351;&#2361; &#2332;&#2381;&#2334;&#2366;&#2340; &#2325;&#2368;&#2332;&#2367;&#2319;&#2404;</p>", "options_en": ["17.25% loss", "17.25% profit", "18.25% profit", "18.75% loss"], "options_hi": ["17.25% &#2361;&#2366;&#2344;&#2367;", "17.25% &#2354;&#2366;&#2349;", "18.25% &#2354;&#2366;&#2349;", "18.75% &#2361;&#2366;&#2344;&#2367;"], "answer": 1, "solution_en": "<p>Cost price for Aarav = &#8377;10000</p><p>Selling price = 115% of 10000 = &#8377;11500</p><p>New cost price = 85% of 11500 = &#8377;9775</p><p>Loss percentage = [(11500  -  9775)/10000]*100 = 17.25% profit</p>", "solution_hi": "<p>Cost price for Aarav = &#8377;10000</p><p>Selling price = 115% of 10000 = &#8377;11500</p><p>New cost price = 85% of 11500 = &#8377;9775</p><p>Loss percentage = [(11500  -  9775)/10000]*100 = 17.25% profit</p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25, "chap": "Percentage"}]}